-- title:
--   Galois action on points versus places for the twisted X₁(Mp) model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K \subseteq L((q))$ be the intermediate field $\operatorname{laurentBaseChange}$ of the function field $\operatorname{x1FunctionField}(Mp) \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of that field. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion $\operatorname{coeffEmb}_L(\operatorname{jq})$; fix compatible embeddings $A \to L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $M\eta$ be a `CurveModel` of $\operatorname{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — an integral scheme, proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with a ring isomorphism of $\operatorname{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ onto its function field over the base, and a bijection of its closed points with the places of that field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ cutting out exactly the valuation subrings. Let $e\eta$ be an isomorphism from $M\eta.C$ to the pullback of $\operatorname{modelTo}_{A,K,j} \colon \operatorname{TwoChartModel}(A,K,j) \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, compatible with the structure morphisms, such that the preimage in $M\eta.C$ of the image of the $j$-finite chart immersion $\operatorname{\iota Fin}_{A,K,j}$ is non-empty, and pinned: for every $a$ in the chart algebra $\operatorname{chartAlgFin}(A,K,j) \subseteq K$, the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ along $e\eta$ followed by the first projection, read through $M\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, is the coefficientwise image under $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $a \in K \subseteq L((q))$. Assume furthermore a multiplicative semiring action of $\operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ on $A$ compatible with $A \to L$, elements $\sigma' \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and $s \in \operatorname{Gal}(L/\mathbb{Q})$ with $\sigma'|_L = s$, an automorphism $w$ of $\operatorname{TwoChartModel}(A,K,j)$ lying over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the action of $s^{-1}$ on $A$, and a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $\operatorname{chartAlgFin}(A,K,j)$ acting on $q$-expansions by applying $s^{-1}$ to coefficients, such that $\operatorname{\iota Fin}$ followed by $w$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}\theta$ followed by $\operatorname{\iota Fin}$. Then for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M\eta$ (sections of $M\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$) satisfying $x'$ followed by $e\eta$ and the first projection $=$ $\operatorname{Spec}\sigma'$ followed by $x$, by $e\eta$, by the first projection and by $w$, the place of $\operatorname{x1FunctionFieldBar}(Mp)$ attached to $x'$ equals the translate by $\operatorname{arithmeticGalois}(\operatorname{x1FunctionField}(Mp))(\sigma')$ — the semilinear automorphism acting coefficientwise by $\sigma'$ — of the place attached to $x$.
--
--   This is the compatibility between the Galois action on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of a model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the action on places of its function field, stated for the full group $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ rather than only for automorphisms fixing $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$: an element moving $\zeta_p$ is realised on the base change of the two-chart model over $A$ by combining $\operatorname{Spec}\sigma'$ on the second factor with the twist $w$ covering $s^{-1}$ on $\operatorname{Spec} A$. It feeds the statements about Hecke and Galois equivariance of the Abel–Jacobi map and of the torsion points used later in the argument.
